[
  {
    "segment_id": "s00001",
    "start_seconds": 0.0,
    "end_seconds": 4.28,
    "text": "Last week, a developer got so tired of"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00002",
    "start_seconds": 2.2,
    "end_seconds": 6.36,
    "text": "Adobe's predatory business model that he"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00003",
    "start_seconds": 4.28,
    "end_seconds": 8.72,
    "text": "decided to rebuild seven of its Creative"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00004",
    "start_seconds": 6.36,
    "end_seconds": 10.440000000000001,
    "text": "Cloud apps with Rust, like Photoshop,"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00005",
    "start_seconds": 8.72,
    "end_seconds": 12.200000000000001,
    "text": "Illustrator, and Premiere, then"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00006",
    "start_seconds": 10.44,
    "end_seconds": 13.879999999999999,
    "text": "open-sourced them, and gave them away"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00007",
    "start_seconds": 12.2,
    "end_seconds": 15.68,
    "text": "for free. The project is called"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00008",
    "start_seconds": 13.88,
    "end_seconds": 17.76,
    "text": "ArtCraft, and the developer's name is"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00009",
    "start_seconds": 15.68,
    "end_seconds": 19.52,
    "text": "Brandon Thomas, who, after being hit"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00010",
    "start_seconds": 17.76,
    "end_seconds": 21.240000000000002,
    "text": "with Adobe's cancellation fee more than"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00011",
    "start_seconds": 19.52,
    "end_seconds": 23.52,
    "text": "once, opened up Claude, then"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00012",
    "start_seconds": 21.24,
    "end_seconds": 25.36,
    "text": "reverse-engineered Adobe's 30-plus-year"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00013",
    "start_seconds": 23.52,
    "end_seconds": 27.56,
    "text": "code base from scratch. And the apps"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00014",
    "start_seconds": 25.36,
    "end_seconds": 29.16,
    "text": "even run on Linux, a platform Adobe has"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00015",
    "start_seconds": 27.56,
    "end_seconds": 30.959999999999997,
    "text": "never officially supported. What's"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00016",
    "start_seconds": 29.16,
    "end_seconds": 32.599000000000004,
    "text": "crazy, though, is that you, the human"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00017",
    "start_seconds": 30.96,
    "end_seconds": 34.4,
    "text": "being watching this video, can do the"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00018",
    "start_seconds": 32.599,
    "end_seconds": 35.31999999999999,
    "text": "same thing thanks to an unrelated"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00019",
    "start_seconds": 34.4,
    "end_seconds": 37.04,
    "text": "project called"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00020",
    "start_seconds": 35.32,
    "end_seconds": 38.68,
    "text": "reverse-engineer-anything. It's been"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00021",
    "start_seconds": 37.04,
    "end_seconds": 40.56,
    "text": "going viral on the internet lately"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00022",
    "start_seconds": 38.68,
    "end_seconds": 42.16,
    "text": "because it can easily decompile any"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00023",
    "start_seconds": 40.56,
    "end_seconds": 44.32,
    "text": "native binaries you can get your hands"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00024",
    "start_seconds": 42.16,
    "end_seconds": 46.67999999999999,
    "text": "on. We're talking stripped ELF, PE, and"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00025",
    "start_seconds": 44.32,
    "end_seconds": 48.12,
    "text": "Mach-O executables, JVM bytecode with"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00026",
    "start_seconds": 46.68,
    "end_seconds": 49.72,
    "text": "obfuscated constant pools,"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00027",
    "start_seconds": 48.12,
    "end_seconds": 51.599999999999994,
    "text": "ECMA-335-compliant"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00028",
    "start_seconds": 49.72,
    "end_seconds": 53.32,
    "text": ".NET assemblies, bare-metal firmware"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00029",
    "start_seconds": 51.6,
    "end_seconds": 55.52,
    "text": "with architecture-specific instruction"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00030",
    "start_seconds": 53.32,
    "end_seconds": 57.24,
    "text": "sets, and even OCI container layers"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00031",
    "start_seconds": 55.52,
    "end_seconds": 59.52,
    "text": "entangled in declarative infrastructure"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00032",
    "start_seconds": 57.24,
    "end_seconds": 61.32,
    "text": "manifests. In layman's terms, that means"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00033",
    "start_seconds": 59.52,
    "end_seconds": 63.2,
    "text": "virtually every app in the world is now"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00034",
    "start_seconds": 61.32,
    "end_seconds": 65.08,
    "text": "open-source, whether it wants to be or"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00035",
    "start_seconds": 63.2,
    "end_seconds": 66.96000000000001,
    "text": "not. In today's video, we'll attempt to"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00036",
    "start_seconds": 65.08,
    "end_seconds": 68.48,
    "text": "reverse-engineer anything and everything"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00037",
    "start_seconds": 66.96,
    "end_seconds": 70.32,
    "text": "and find out if this is the final nail"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00038",
    "start_seconds": 68.48,
    "end_seconds": 72.88000000000001,
    "text": "in the coffin for software as we know"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00039",
    "start_seconds": 70.32,
    "end_seconds": 74.6,
    "text": "it. It is October 12th, 2026, and you're"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00040",
    "start_seconds": 72.88,
    "end_seconds": 77.0,
    "text": "watching The Code Report. So, is it"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00041",
    "start_seconds": 74.6,
    "end_seconds": 78.96,
    "text": "really true that one person plus Claude"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00042",
    "start_seconds": 77.0,
    "end_seconds": 81.52,
    "text": "made the entire Adobe suite obsolete"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00043",
    "start_seconds": 78.96,
    "end_seconds": 83.0,
    "text": "overnight? Well, on the surface, yes. As"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00044",
    "start_seconds": 81.52,
    "end_seconds": 84.64,
    "text": "you can see on the website, you can"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00045",
    "start_seconds": 83.0,
    "end_seconds": 86.92,
    "text": "download a Rust-based version of any"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00046",
    "start_seconds": 84.64,
    "end_seconds": 89.2,
    "text": "Adobe program for free right now. That's"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00047",
    "start_seconds": 86.92,
    "end_seconds": 91.2,
    "text": "awesome, but after trying it out myself,"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00048",
    "start_seconds": 89.2,
    "end_seconds": 93.44,
    "text": "I realized there's one small catch. The"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00049",
    "start_seconds": 91.2,
    "end_seconds": 94.92,
    "text": "software is a nearly unusable pile of"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00050",
    "start_seconds": 93.44,
    "end_seconds": 97.24,
    "text": "vibe-coded horse Now, I"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00051",
    "start_seconds": 94.92,
    "end_seconds": 98.68,
    "text": "begrudgingly pay Adobe a $69 tribute"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00052",
    "start_seconds": 97.24,
    "end_seconds": 100.39999999999999,
    "text": "every month to use Premiere to edit"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00053",
    "start_seconds": 98.68,
    "end_seconds": 101.84,
    "text": "these videos for you guys, and I was"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00054",
    "start_seconds": 100.4,
    "end_seconds": 103.4,
    "text": "thrilled to finally see an open-source"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00055",
    "start_seconds": 101.84,
    "end_seconds": 104.96000000000001,
    "text": "alternative. And let's just ignore the"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00056",
    "start_seconds": 103.4,
    "end_seconds": 106.60000000000001,
    "text": "fact that DaVinci Resolve has been an"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00057",
    "start_seconds": 104.96,
    "end_seconds": 108.08,
    "text": "open-source alternative for over 20"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00058",
    "start_seconds": 106.6,
    "end_seconds": 109.75999999999999,
    "text": "years now. And when I first opened"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00059",
    "start_seconds": 108.08,
    "end_seconds": 112.0,
    "text": "FilmCraft, I was thrilled to see that"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00060",
    "start_seconds": 109.76,
    "end_seconds": 113.4,
    "text": "the UI was nearly a one-to-one clone of"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00061",
    "start_seconds": 112.0,
    "end_seconds": 115.2,
    "text": "Premiere. So, I could get to work"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00062",
    "start_seconds": 113.4,
    "end_seconds": 117.28,
    "text": "immediately without any learning curve."
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00063",
    "start_seconds": 115.2,
    "end_seconds": 118.72,
    "text": "My plan was to edit this video with it,"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00064",
    "start_seconds": 117.28,
    "end_seconds": 120.88,
    "text": "but the cracks became visible"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00065",
    "start_seconds": 118.72,
    "end_seconds": 122.48,
    "text": "immediately. Like after dragging a clip"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00066",
    "start_seconds": 120.88,
    "end_seconds": 124.56,
    "text": "of some lame stock video onto the"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00067",
    "start_seconds": 122.48,
    "end_seconds": 126.80000000000001,
    "text": "timeline and hitting play, there was a"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00068",
    "start_seconds": 124.56,
    "end_seconds": 128.8,
    "text": "massive lag in the audio bars and just"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00069",
    "start_seconds": 126.8,
    "end_seconds": 130.47899999999998,
    "text": "overall slowness and laziness despite"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00070",
    "start_seconds": 128.8,
    "end_seconds": 131.959,
    "text": "being vibe coded in rust, which I've"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00071",
    "start_seconds": 130.479,
    "end_seconds": 134.04000000000002,
    "text": "been told is a blazingly fast"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00072",
    "start_seconds": 131.959,
    "end_seconds": 135.84,
    "text": "programming language. So then, I tried"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00073",
    "start_seconds": 134.04,
    "end_seconds": 137.32,
    "text": "implementing some transitions between"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00074",
    "start_seconds": 135.84,
    "end_seconds": 138.959,
    "text": "clips and they were just nowhere near"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00075",
    "start_seconds": 137.32,
    "end_seconds": 140.79999999999998,
    "text": "the quality of Premiere, which you can"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00076",
    "start_seconds": 138.959,
    "end_seconds": 142.68,
    "text": "clearly see with this glitch transition"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00077",
    "start_seconds": 140.8,
    "end_seconds": 144.48000000000002,
    "text": "side-by-side. And for someone like me"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00078",
    "start_seconds": 142.68,
    "end_seconds": 145.92000000000002,
    "text": "who's a once-in-a-generation cinematic"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00079",
    "start_seconds": 144.48,
    "end_seconds": 148.04,
    "text": "visionary who many have called the"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00080",
    "start_seconds": 145.92,
    "end_seconds": 150.23999999999998,
    "text": "Stanley Kubrick of sponsored posts,"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00081",
    "start_seconds": 148.04,
    "end_seconds": 151.56,
    "text": "the sad reality is that Film Craft is"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00082",
    "start_seconds": 150.24,
    "end_seconds": 153.20000000000002,
    "text": "just not good enough yet. But I"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00083",
    "start_seconds": 151.56,
    "end_seconds": 155.48,
    "text": "sincerely hope it gets there someday"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00084",
    "start_seconds": 153.2,
    "end_seconds": 157.11999999999998,
    "text": "because Adobe. But then that got me"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00085",
    "start_seconds": 155.48,
    "end_seconds": 159.11999999999998,
    "text": "thinking, what if instead of trying to"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00086",
    "start_seconds": 157.12,
    "end_seconds": 161.20000000000002,
    "text": "use off-brand Premiere, I just reverse"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00087",
    "start_seconds": 159.12,
    "end_seconds": 162.6,
    "text": "engineer it myself and make it simpler"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00088",
    "start_seconds": 161.2,
    "end_seconds": 164.39999999999998,
    "text": "because Premiere has hundreds of"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00089",
    "start_seconds": 162.6,
    "end_seconds": 165.959,
    "text": "features that I don't use that just get"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00090",
    "start_seconds": 164.4,
    "end_seconds": 167.88,
    "text": "in the way. Luckily, there's a new"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00091",
    "start_seconds": 165.959,
    "end_seconds": 169.84,
    "text": "project in town that can help us do that"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00092",
    "start_seconds": 167.88,
    "end_seconds": 171.84,
    "text": "called reverse engineer anything. Adobe"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00093",
    "start_seconds": 169.84,
    "end_seconds": 174.68,
    "text": "Premiere is primarily written in C and"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00094",
    "start_seconds": 171.84,
    "end_seconds": 176.04,
    "text": "C++, and crazy smart Asians on H-1B"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00095",
    "start_seconds": 174.68,
    "end_seconds": 178.32,
    "text": "visas have been writing its code for"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00096",
    "start_seconds": 176.04,
    "end_seconds": 180.76,
    "text": "decades. Now, its actual source code is"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00097",
    "start_seconds": 178.32,
    "end_seconds": 182.32,
    "text": "top secret Adobe intellectual property,"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00098",
    "start_seconds": 180.76,
    "end_seconds": 184.44,
    "text": "but in order to actually run it on your"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00099",
    "start_seconds": 182.32,
    "end_seconds": 186.84,
    "text": "machine, they need to compile that code"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00100",
    "start_seconds": 184.44,
    "end_seconds": 188.44,
    "text": "into a native binary of ones and zeros."
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00101",
    "start_seconds": 186.84,
    "end_seconds": 190.56,
    "text": "This stuff is almost unreadable to"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00102",
    "start_seconds": 188.44,
    "end_seconds": 192.76,
    "text": "humans, but with a lot of painstaking"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00103",
    "start_seconds": 190.56,
    "end_seconds": 194.6,
    "text": "work, it is technically possible to map"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00104",
    "start_seconds": 192.76,
    "end_seconds": 196.239,
    "text": "these ones and zeros back into something"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00105",
    "start_seconds": 194.6,
    "end_seconds": 198.35999999999999,
    "text": "that resembles human readable source"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00106",
    "start_seconds": 196.239,
    "end_seconds": 200.08,
    "text": "code. And the REA project can do that"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00107",
    "start_seconds": 198.36,
    "end_seconds": 202.12,
    "text": "for people who can't even count to three"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00108",
    "start_seconds": 200.08,
    "end_seconds": 204.44000000000003,
    "text": "in binary. First, we set it up by"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00109",
    "start_seconds": 202.12,
    "end_seconds": 206.20000000000002,
    "text": "running it with Node.js and the NPX"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00110",
    "start_seconds": 204.44,
    "end_seconds": 208.519,
    "text": "command. And then because I'm a loser on"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00111",
    "start_seconds": 206.2,
    "end_seconds": 210.56,
    "text": "Microsoft Windows, we'll configure REA's"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00112",
    "start_seconds": 208.519,
    "end_seconds": 211.88,
    "text": "Ghidra integration, which is actually"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00113",
    "start_seconds": 210.56,
    "end_seconds": 214.36,
    "text": "the tool that deserves the most credit"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00114",
    "start_seconds": 211.88,
    "end_seconds": 217.0,
    "text": "here and can do a read-only analysis of"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00115",
    "start_seconds": 214.36,
    "end_seconds": 218.959,
    "text": "native EXEs and DLLs. Then from there,"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00116",
    "start_seconds": 217.0,
    "end_seconds": 220.84,
    "text": "we can just use it like any other AI"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00117",
    "start_seconds": 218.959,
    "end_seconds": 222.68,
    "text": "agent and tell it to inspect the locally"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00118",
    "start_seconds": 220.84,
    "end_seconds": 224.32,
    "text": "installed version of Adobe Premiere. In"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00119",
    "start_seconds": 222.68,
    "end_seconds": 226.32,
    "text": "this case, I'll have it inspect Adobe's"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00120",
    "start_seconds": 224.32,
    "end_seconds": 227.79999999999998,
    "text": "timeline integration and try to figure"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00121",
    "start_seconds": 226.32,
    "end_seconds": 229.76,
    "text": "out how it does this one specific"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00122",
    "start_seconds": 227.8,
    "end_seconds": 231.96,
    "text": "feature. A while later, we get back a"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00123",
    "start_seconds": 229.76,
    "end_seconds": 234.0,
    "text": "bunch of C-like pseudo code along with"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00124",
    "start_seconds": 231.96,
    "end_seconds": 236.32000000000002,
    "text": "assembly, strings, symbols, calls, and"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00125",
    "start_seconds": 234.0,
    "end_seconds": 238.24,
    "text": "references, which to an obsolete HTML"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00126",
    "start_seconds": 236.32,
    "end_seconds": 239.92,
    "text": "programmer is all pretty useless."
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00127",
    "start_seconds": 238.24,
    "end_seconds": 241.72,
    "text": "However, we can now take this garbage"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00128",
    "start_seconds": 239.92,
    "end_seconds": 243.95999999999998,
    "text": "code and pass it off to our favorite"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00129",
    "start_seconds": 241.72,
    "end_seconds": 245.76,
    "text": "coding agent to re-implement the exact"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00130",
    "start_seconds": 243.96,
    "end_seconds": 247.52,
    "text": "same feature in Rust. And thanks to"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00131",
    "start_seconds": 245.76,
    "end_seconds": 249.23999999999998,
    "text": "reverse engineering, I'll eventually be"
  },
  {
    "segment_id": "s00132",
    "start_seconds": 247.52,
    "end_seconds": 251.56,
